    "title": "Air Jordan 12 Retro PSNY 'Bordeaux' - A Full-Bodied Classic: Where to Buy Now - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Porcha Mazique ,\n20 minutes ago\nThe Air Jordan 12 Retro PSNY ‘Bordeaux’ is smooth in the way only something aged to perfection can be. That deep wine hue has the same richness as a glass of Bordeaux, and that’s what makes this sneaker special. The vibe feels refined yet bold enough to make a statement.\nThe story behind this particular pair is just as important as its color. Public School New York (PSNY) teamed up with Jordan Brand for a full monochromatic collection of the AJ12, and the ‘Bordeaux’ colorway instantly stood out. It wasn’t just about dressing the silhouette in a new shade—it was about elevating it.\nAir Jordan 12 Retro PSNY BordeauxNike\nThe wine-inspired color ties back to the Air Jordan 7, which first introduced Bordeaux into the Jordan line. But here, instead of mixing tones, the PSNY collab doubled down with lush suede across the entire upper. The result? A sneaker that feels less like sportswear and more like something you’d find in a designer showroom.\nStyle Code: AA1233-600 Colorway: Bordeaux/Bordeaux Original Price: $300 Release Date: 6/28/2017 Where to Buy: Novelship Of course, with that kind of elegance, the Bordeaux 12s aren’t really a “daily wear” for me. These are closer to a grail piece—something you pull out sparingly, because wearing them feels like an occasion in itself. I’d probably reserve them for special occasions or those moments when I want to add a bit of drama to my look.\nWhat I like most about these 12s is that they feel luxurious, almost like an accessory that carries the same weight as a leather bag or a tailored jacket. They’re refined, full-bodied, and meant to be savored—just like the wine they’re named after.\nRelated: Air Jordan 12 Retro ‘Deadly Pink’ — Bold Presence, Hot Pink Energy: Where to Buy Now\nRelated: Air Jordan 12 Retro 'Black Taxi' — A Quiet Flex on Your Feet, Here's Where to Buy Now\n2",
